This is strange. The execute tool is creating new request entities each time, but they all return 404 with empty bodies. Let me try a very small test call to see what's happening. Perhaps the URL parameter is missing.

Actually, the response says `"detail": "Not Found"` — maybe the server can't route my request properly? The OpenAPI spec says the server is at http://localhost:9001 and the paths are /v3/cargo-manifests, /v2/cargo etc.

But the OpenAPI also mentioned paths /v3/oauth/token. Maybe I need to call that first? But the task says the token is in the workspace already. Let me look more carefully at the spec to see how to authenticate.

The spec says:
```
"/v3/oauth/token": {
  "post": {
    "summary": "OAuth client_credentials",
    "security": [
      {
        "none": []
      }
    ]
  }
},
```

So /v3/oauth/token has no security which means it's open. All other endpoints have bearer security.

Let me try executing with the bearer token properly. Let me check what's coming through by reading one of my request entities.
